      "content": "The three numbers on your fertilizer bag represent the percentage of Nitrogen, Phosphorus, and Potassium it contains. For your yellowing lawn, the first number (Nitrogen) is the most critical because low levels directly cause thinning and yellowing, whereas other deficiencies often make leaves dark green but small or pale green. Since your grass doesn't seem dark green, it is likely a Nitrogen issue, making a balanced 10-10-10 fertilizer a safe starting point until you can confirm the specific missing nutrient.",
